   "source": [
    "# 🚀 Data Engineering Pipeline Tutorial - Part 2\n",
    "## S3 Data Lake & Data Cleansing\n",
    "\n",
    "### What Actually Happened in Our Pipeline:\n",
    "```\n",
    "Bronze Zone (5 files uploaded):\n",
    "├── bronze/mysql_customers/year=2026/month=01/day=19/*.parquet\n",
    "├── bronze/mysql_orders/year=2026/month=01/day=19/*.parquet\n",
    "├── bronze/customers/year=2026/month=01/day=19/*.csv\n",
    "├── bronze/products/year=2026/month=01/day=19/*.csv\n",
    "└── bronze/exchange_rates/year=2026/month=01/day=19/*.json\n",
    "\n",
    "Silver Zone (5 files - all converted to parquet):\n",
    "└── silver/*/year=2026/month=01/day=19/*.parquet\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## ☁️ Part 4: S3 Data Lake Operations\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why MinIO for Local Data Lakes?\n",
    "| Feature | Benefit |\n",
    "|---------|--------|\n",
    "| Cost | ~Free (local) (very cheap) |\n",
    "| Durability | 99.999999999% (11 nines) |\n",
    "| Scalability | Unlimited storage |\n",
    "| Integration | S3-compatible API, works with any S3 tools |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Medallion Architecture\n",
    "```\n",
    "BRONZE          →        SILVER         →        GOLD\n",
    "Raw data                 Cleaned                 Business-ready\n",
    "Multiple formats         Parquet only            Aggregated\n",
    "As-is from source        Validated               Transformed\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import boto3\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import io\n",
    "from datetime import datetime\n",
    "\n",
    "class S3Handler:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Handle S3 operations for data lake.\n",
    "    This is the actual class from our working pipeline!\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def __init__(self, bucket: str, region: str = \"ap-southeast-2\"):\n",
    "        self.bucket = bucket\n",
    "        # boto3.client = low-level AWS service client\n",
    "        self.s3 = boto3.client("s3", endpoint_url="http://tina-minio:9000", region_name=region)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def _generate_path(self, zone: str, source: str, file_format: str) -> str:\n",
    "        \"\"\"\n",
    "        Generate S3 path with DATE PARTITIONING.\n",
    "        \n",
    "        Why partition by date?\n",
    "        - Query efficiency: Only scan relevant data\n",
    "        - Cost savings: Less data scanned = lower Athena costs\n",
    "        - Data management: Easy retention policies\n",
    "        \n",
    "        Output example:\n",
    "        bronze/mysql_customers/year=2026/month=01/day=19/mysql_customers_210741.parquet\n",
    "        \n",
    "        The year=/month=/day= format is \"Hive-style partitioning\"\n",
    "        - Works automatically with AWS Athena, Glue, Spark\n",
    "        \"\"\"\n",
    "        now = datetime.now()\n",
    "        # :02d = format as 2 digits with leading zero (01, 02, ... 12)\n",
    "        return f\"{zone}/{source}/year={now.year}/month={now.month:02d}/day={now.day:02d}/{source}_{now.strftime('%H%M%S')}.{file_format}\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def upload_to_bronze(self, df: pd.DataFrame, source_name: str, \n",
    "                         file_format: str = \"parquet\") -> str:\n",
    "        \"\"\"\n",
    "        Upload raw data to Bronze zone.\n",
    "        \n",
    "        Why Parquet format?\n",
    "        - Columnar: Fast for analytics (read only needed columns)\n",
    "        - Compressed: 75% smaller than CSV typically\n",
    "        - Schema embedded: Self-describing\n",
    "        - Industry standard: Works everywhere\n",
    "        \"\"\"\n",
    "        s3_path = self._generate_path(\"bronze\", source_name, file_format)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # io.BytesIO = in-memory binary stream\n",
    "        # Avoids creating temporary files on disk\n",
    "        buffer = io.BytesIO()\n",
    "        \n",
    "        if file_format == \"parquet\":\n",
    "            df.to_parquet(buffer, index=False)\n",
    "        elif file_format == \"csv\":\n",
    "            csv_data = df.to_csv(index=False)\n",
    "            buffer = io.BytesIO(csv_data.encode('utf-8'))\n",
    "        elif file_format == \"json\":\n",
    "            json_data = df.to_json(orient='records')\n",
    "            buffer = io.BytesIO(json_data.encode('utf-8'))\n",
    "        \n",
    "        buffer.seek(0)  # Reset pointer to start\n",
    "        self.s3.upload_fileobj(buffer, self.bucket, s3_path)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        print(f\"✅ Uploaded: s3://{self.bucket}/{s3_path}\")\n",
    "        return s3_path\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def read_parquet(self, s3_path: str) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "        \"\"\"Read parquet file from S3 into DataFrame.\"\"\"\n",
    "        response = self.s3.get_object(Bucket=self.bucket, Key=s3_path)\n",
    "        return pd.read_parquet(io.BytesIO(response['Body'].read()))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def list_files(self, prefix: str) -> list:\n",
    "        \"\"\"List files in S3 path.\"\"\"\n",
    "        response = self.s3.list_objects_v2(Bucket=self.bucket, Prefix=prefix)\n",
    "        return [obj['Key'] for obj in response.get('Contents', [])]\n",
    "\n",
    "# ACTUAL USAGE - Your real bucket!\n",
    "s3 = S3Handler(\"data-lake\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# List what's in your bucket\n",
    "print(\"📁 Bronze zone files:\")\n",
    "for f in s3.list_files(\"bronze/\")[:5]:\n",
    "    print(f\"   {f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 💡 S3 Path Best Practices\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "s3://data-lake/bronze/mysql_customers/year=2026/month=01/day=19/file.parquet\n",
    "     └─────────bucket─────────┘ └zone┘ └───source────┘ └────partitions─────┘ └──file──┘\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Partition columns in path = automatic filtering in Athena:**\n",
    "```sql\n",
    "-- This only scans January 2026 data, not entire bucket!\n",
    "SELECT * FROM bronze_customers \n",
    "WHERE year = 2026 AND month = 1;\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 🧹 Part 5: Data Cleansing (Bronze → Silver)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Silver zone = trusted data.** Clean once, use everywhere.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Common Data Quality Issues We Handle:\n",
    "1. Duplicate rows\n",
    "2. Null/missing values\n",
    "3. Inconsistent column names\n",
    "4. Wrong data types\n",
    "5. Whitespace in strings"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from typing import Dict, List, Callable\n",
    "\n",
    "class DataCleaner:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Data cleansing utilities for Silver zone.\n",
    "    Actual code from our working pipeline!\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    @staticmethod\n",
    "    def remove_duplicates(df: pd.DataFrame, subset: List[str] = None) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "        \"\"\"\n",
    "        Remove duplicate rows.\n",
    "        \n",
    "        subset: columns to check (None = all columns)\n",
    "        \"\"\"\n",
    "        before = len(df)\n",
    "        df = df.drop_duplicates(subset=subset)\n",
    "        removed = before - len(df)\n",
    "        if removed > 0:\n",
    "            print(f\"🗑️ Removed {removed} duplicate rows\")\n",
    "        return df\n",
    "    \n",
    "    @staticmethod\n",
    "    def standardize_columns(df: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "        \"\"\"\n",
    "        Standardize column names: lowercase, underscores.\n",
    "        \n",
    "        'Customer Name' → 'customer_name'\n",
    "        'Order-ID' → 'order_id'\n",
    "        \n",
    "        Why? Consistent naming across all data sources.\n",
    "        \"\"\"\n",
    "        df.columns = (df.columns\n",
    "                      .str.lower()\n",
    "                      .str.replace(' ', '_')\n",
    "                      .str.replace('-', '_'))\n",
    "        return df\n",
    "    \n",
    "    @staticmethod\n",
    "    def handle_nulls(df: pd.DataFrame, strategy: Dict[str, str]) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "        \"\"\"\n",
    "        Handle null values with different strategies per column.\n",
    "        \n",
    "        Strategies:\n",
    "        - 'drop': Remove rows with nulls in this column\n",
    "        - 'mean': Fill with column mean (numeric only)\n",
    "        - 'median': Fill with column median\n",
    "        - 'mode': Fill with most common value\n",
    "        - 'zero': Fill with 0\n",
    "        - 'empty': Fill with empty string\n",
    "        \n",
    "        Example: {'email': 'empty', 'price': 'mean'}\n",
    "        \"\"\"\n",
    "        for col, method in strategy.items():\n",
    "            if col not in df.columns:\n",
    "                continue\n",
    "            \n",
    "            null_count = df[col].isnull().sum()\n",
    "            if null_count == 0:\n",
    "                continue\n",
    "            \n",
    "            if method == 'drop':\n",
    "                df = df.dropna(subset=[col])\n",
    "            elif method == 'mean':\n",
    "                df[col] = df[col].fillna(df[col].mean())\n",
    "            elif method == 'median':\n",
    "                df[col] = df[col].fillna(df[col].median())\n",
    "            elif method == 'mode':\n",
    "                df[col] = df[col].fillna(df[col].mode()[0])\n",
    "            elif method == 'zero':\n",
    "                df[col] = df[col].fillna(0)\n",
    "            elif method == 'empty':\n",
    "                df[col] = df[col].fillna('')\n",
    "            \n",
    "            print(f\"🔧 Handled {null_count} nulls in '{col}' using '{method}'\")\n",
    "        \n",
    "        return df\n",
    "    \n",
    "    @staticmethod\n",
    "    def convert_types(df: pd.DataFrame, type_map: Dict[str, str]) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "        \"\"\"\n",
    "        Convert column data types.\n",
    "        \n",
    "        type_map: {'order_date': 'datetime', 'amount': 'float'}\n",
    "        \"\"\"\n",
    "        for col, dtype in type_map.items():\n",
    "            if col not in df.columns:\n",
    "                continue\n",
    "            try:\n",
    "                if dtype == 'datetime':\n",
    "                    df[col] = pd.to_datetime(df[col], errors='coerce')\n",
    "                elif dtype == 'float':\n",
    "                    df[col] = pd.to_numeric(df[col], errors='coerce')\n",
    "                elif dtype == 'int':\n",
    "                    df[col] = pd.to_numeric(df[col], errors='coerce').astype('Int64')\n",
    "                print(f\"✅ Converted '{col}' to {dtype}\")\n",
    "            except Exception as e:\n",
    "                print(f\"⚠️ Failed to convert {col}: {e}\")\n",
    "        return df\n",
    "    \n",
    "    @staticmethod\n",
    "    def trim_strings(df: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "        \"\"\"Remove leading/trailing whitespace from string columns.\"\"\"\n",
    "        str_cols = df.select_dtypes(include=['object']).columns\n",
    "        for col in str_cols:\n",
    "            try:\n",
    "                df[col] = df[col].astype(str).str.strip()\n",
    "            except:\n",
    "                pass\n",
    "        return df"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# DEMO: Data Cleansing in Action\n",
    "# This simulates what our pipeline does to Bronze data\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create messy sample data (like raw Bronze data)\n",
    "messy_data = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    'Customer Name': ['  Alice  ', 'Bob', 'Alice', 'Charlie', None],\n",
    "    'Email': ['alice@email.com', 'bob@email.com', 'alice@email.com', None, 'eve@email.com'],\n",
    "    'Order-Amount': ['100.50', '-50', '100.50', '200', '150'],\n",
    "    'Order Date': ['2026-01-15', '2026-01-16', '2026-01-15', '2026-01-17', '2026-01-18']\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"❌ BEFORE CLEANING (Bronze):\")\n",
    "print(messy_data)\n",
    "print(f\"\\nColumns: {list(messy_data.columns)}\")\n",
    "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\"*60 + \"\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "cleaner = DataCleaner()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Step 1: Standardize column names\n",
    "df = cleaner.standardize_columns(messy_data.copy())\n",
    "print(f\"Step 1 - Columns now: {list(df.columns)}\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Step 2: Remove duplicates\n",
    "df = cleaner.remove_duplicates(df, subset=['customer_name', 'order_date'])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Step 3: Handle nulls\n",
    "df = cleaner.handle_nulls(df, {\n",
    "    'customer_name': 'drop',  # Remove rows with no name\n",
    "    'email': 'empty'          # Fill missing emails with ''\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "# Step 4: Convert types\n",
    "df = cleaner.convert_types(df, {\n",
    "    'order_date': 'datetime',\n",
    "    'order_amount': 'float'\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "# Step 5: Trim strings\n",
    "df = cleaner.trim_strings(df)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\"*60)\n",
    "print(\"✅ AFTER CLEANING (Silver):\")\n",
    "print(df)\n",
    "print(f\"\\nData types:\\n{df.dtypes}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 🎯 Lambda Functions for Validation\n",
    "\n",
    "**Lambda** = anonymous one-line function\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "# Regular function\n",
    "def is_positive(x):\n",
    "    return x > 0\n",
    "\n",
    "# Same as lambda\n",
    "is_positive = lambda x: x > 0\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Common validation lambdas:**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Validation rules using lambda functions\n",
    "validation_rules = {\n",
    "    'email': lambda x: '@' in str(x),           # Must contain @\n",
    "    'price': lambda x: x > 0,                   # Must be positive\n",
    "    'age': lambda x: 0 < x < 150,               # Reasonable age\n",
    "    'quantity': lambda x: x >= 0,               # Non-negative\n",
    "    'status': lambda x: x in ['active', 'inactive'],  # Valid values\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test them\n",
    "print(\"Testing validation rules:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  email 'test@email.com': {validation_rules['email']('test@email.com')}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  email 'invalid': {validation_rules['email']('invalid')}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  price 100: {validation_rules['price'](100)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  price -50: {validation_rules['price'](-50)}\")"
   ]
